I've released an updated version of my "K Reform" patch, which lessens
the number of ambiguous monster ASCII symbol/color combinations by
spilling some monster types from "@" (humans) to "K" (Keystone Kops).
Assuming I've made no mistakes, the only gameplay difference is the
implications of blessed genocide.

In the previous version, although Croesus is not a cop, I moved him to
keep him together with his guards.  For this patch, I thought of a better
rationalization -- K now represents "Kops and Kapitalists" (although I use
non-anarchist spelling in the game itself...) So Shopkeepers go in too.

One of the comments on the previous versions was that Croesus really
should be purple since he is a "regal" monster.  I knew that, but magenta
was already taken.  This round, I've elected to displace the Kop Kaptain
to Light Cyan so that Croesus can get the spot.

Also, this time I resolved the Keystone Kop / Kop Sergeant ambiguity by
making the Sergeant Light Blue.  (Last time, I made the ordinary Kop
black, but that shows the same as blue on many builds of TTY nethack.)

After the patch, the contents of the class are:

 Blue K:        Keystone Kop
 Light Blue K:  Kop Sergeant
 Cyan K:        Kop Lieutenant
 Light Cyan K:  Kop Kaptain
 Gray K:        (minetown) Watchman
 Green K:       (minetown) Watch captain
 Yellow K:      (vault) Guard
 Magenta K:     Croesus
 White K:       Shopkeeper

It's on ftp.ocis.net as
"/pub/users/ldeutsch/beta/nethack-3.4.3-kreform-1.diff".

